":["###Traitement des valeurs aberrantes du Dataframe df_client_sans_just_eat"],"metadata":{"id":"nAXZ1EYJRlkc"},"id":"nAXZ1EYJRlkc"},{"cell_type":"code","source":["# Sélectionnons automatiquement toutes les colonnes numériques\n","variables_numeriques_client = df_client_sans_just_eat.select_dtypes(\n","    include='number'\n",").columns\n","\n","# Parcourons chaque variable numérique\n","for variable in variables_numeriques_client:\n","\n","    # Calcul du premier quartile (Q1)\n","    Q1 = df_client_sans_just_eat[variable].quantile(0.25)\n","\n","    # Calcul du troisième quartile (Q3)\n","    Q3 = df_client_sans_just_eat[variable].quantile(0.75)\n","\n","    # Calcul de l'écart interquartile (IQR)\n","    IQR = Q3 - Q1\n","\n","    # Calcul des bornes de détection des valeurs potentiellement aberrantes\n","    borne_inf = Q1 - 1.5 * IQR\n","    borne_sup = Q3 + 1.5 * IQR\n","\n","    # Compte des valeurs situées en dehors des bornes\n","    nb_aberrantes = (\n","        (df_client_sans_just_eat[variable] < borne_inf) |\n","        (df_client_sans_just_eat[variable] > borne_sup)\n","    ).sum()\n","\n","    # Affichons les résultats\n","    print(\n","        variable,\n","        \"→\",\n","        nb_aberrantes,\n","        \"valeurs potentiellement aberrantes\"\n","    )"],"metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/"},"id":"jkH-UA8lOlaC","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1787927838304,"user_tz":-120,"elapsed":23,"user":{"displayName":"laurent mike","userId":"02027094166112703367"}},"outputId":"72f7f567-066d-4c49-d82b-81a232402fee"},"id":"jkH-UA8lOlaC","execution_count":119,"outputs":[{"output_type":"stream","name":"stdout","text":["count_customers → 21 valeurs potentiellement aberrantes\n"]}]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["Tout d'abord, nous constation que le nombre de valeurs potentiellement aberrantes est passe de 31 à 21 après exclusion des commandes \"Just Eat\".\n","\n","Ensuite, nous avions remarqué  lors de l'audit des données,